# A mark must never be the thing standing in front of what it proves, and the
# body must read in every pose (docs/ART.md §5, §7). Every frame here is at PLAY
# zoom, because that is the only size that counts: a mark that only behaves in a
# close shot is not fixed.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/marks.tour --seed=1 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 \
#     --fit=scanner_lens,boots_magnet,mod_spring
# Each pair is a control frame and then the mark, from the same place, so what
# the mark added to the picture can be counted and not argued about.
coast calm

# --- A blow leaves the machine standing there --------------------------------
# Shot on the first frame after the blow, inside the flash: the struck plate is
# paper, the rest of the body is still its own violet, and its lens is still
# amber. (The flash is 60 ms; a `wait` here would shoot after it.)
place pinewood
wait 1.0
spawn watcher
wait 1.2
shot 01-before-the-blow
try 16
walkto part 1.6
tap swing
await hit 1.8
end
shot 02-the-blow-leaves-it-standing

# --- The machine's own light is smaller than the machine ----------------------
# Its working part at night, at the distance it is read from: a ring of loose
# amber pixels round the part, never a disc wider than the body wearing it.
coast calm
wait 0.4
place coast
hour 22
weather clear:0
wait 1.2
spawn watcher
wait 1.6
shot 03-its-light-is-smaller-than-it-is

# --- A read through a stolen lens, over the thing it reads --------------------
tap ability_scan
await ability:scan 5
wait 0.4
shot 04-read-over-the-thing-it-reads

# --- The dash leaves the body showing ----------------------------------------
# Speed lines are ink over the world, laid where the body WAS: the player must
# still be a person at the head of them.
coast calm
wait 0.5
hour 11
weather clear:0
place coast
wait 1.4
shot 05-before-the-dash
tap ability_dash
await ability:dash 5
wait 0.03
shot 06-the-dash-leaves-the-body-showing

# --- The magnet line is a line -----------------------------------------------
place tip
wait 0.8
walk -1,-1 1.8
walk 1,1 0.25
shot 07-across-from-a-tip
tap ability_grapple
await ability:grapple 5
shot 08-the-line-takes-hold
wait 0.45
shot 09-and-it-shortens

# --- Crouched, still a person ------------------------------------------------
coast calm
wait 0.4
ground heath
wait 1.0
shot 10-standing-in-the-heather
hold crouch
await crouched 3
wait 0.6
shot 11-down-in-the-heather
walk 1,0 0.5
shot 12-and-moving-down-there
# And closer than anyone plays, which is where the art review found it: the
# pose has to hold up under a magnifying glass as well as at 640x360.
zoom 6
wait 0.5
shot 13-down-in-the-heather-close
release crouch
wait 0.5
shot 14-and-up-again-close
zoom 15
wait 0.4

# --- Breath steps off the snow -----------------------------------------------
# The cue fires on its own beat and hangs a second and a half, so the frame is
# taken right after the cold is first felt (the first cue is due at once) and
# again a beat later: breath has to be visible on white ground in both.
place snowfield
hour 19
weather clear:0
wait 1.6
await cold 12
await pressure_bites 15
await breath 10
wait 0.15
shot 15-breath-on-white-ground
wait 2.0
await breath 10
wait 0.6
shot 16-and-the-next-breath
